  "sort": 0,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You shape-shift into a Tree of Life form that looks like a treant, and you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Tree Form.</strong> You become Large. Your Speed becomes 10 feet and can’t be reduced, and &amp;Reference[difficultterrain apply=false]{Difficult Terrain} doesn’t cost you extra movement.</p><p><strong>Bark Skin.</strong> You gain a +2 bonus to Armor Class and 10 Temporary Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Condition Immunity.</strong> You have Immunity to the &amp;Reference[paralyzed apply=false]{Paralyzed} and &amp;Reference[restrained apply=false]{Restrained} conditions, and you can’t be shape-shifted against your will.</p><p><strong>Source of Life.</strong> When a spell you cast with a spell slot restores Hit Points to a creature, that creature regains an extra 1d8 Hit Points on the turn you cast it.</p><p><strong>Spells Enhanced.</strong> The spell save DC of your Druid spells increases by 1, and you have Advantage on the attack rolls of the Druid spells you cast.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-YMZhhBuRHaFrSoLG\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>The effect raises the save DC of all your spells by 1 (only your Druid spells benefit); take the Advantage of Spells Enhanced and the extra 1d8 of Source of Life by hand.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
